  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ADDRESSING POACHING AND WILDLIFE TRAFFICKING IN JEANNETTE KAWAS NATIONAL PARK: COMMUNITY SURVEILLANCE AND URBAN COMMUNICATIONS CAMPAIGN</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to improve wildlife security in Jeannette Kawas National Park in Honduras by strengthening conservation capacity of governmental entities, local communities, and other key stakeholders to reduce poaching and wildlife trafficking. The project is intended to conserve iguanas, freshwater turtles, and peccaries, which indirectly increases the natural prey base of jaguars and reduces human-jaguar conflict.</narrative>
  </description>
